drome between men and women. The diarrheadominant type was more common in men while, constipation-dominant or alternating types were more common in women (<italic>p</italic>&#x0003c;0.001).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-22-851-g002"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Prevalence of gastrointestinal symptoms in women with different menstrual phase</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-22-851-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>NS, not significant.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>